---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Buzzyfly"
	description="Buzzyfly is a small, practical publication about building better workflows — real systems and templates, no fluff."
	pubDate={new Date('August 08 2021')}
	heroImage="/blog-placeholder-about.jpg"
>
	<p>
		Buzzyfly started as a personal notebook — a place to write down the small systems, templates,
		and workarounds that made work feel less chaotic. It's grown into a publication, but the goal
		hasn't changed: help people build workflows that actually hold up under real deadlines.
	</p>

	<h2>What Buzzyfly is</h2>
	<p>
		This is not a productivity blog full of theory and 3,000-word listicles. Every dispatch is
		built around something you can use immediately — a template, a checklist, a script, a process
		that's been tested on a real project before it ever gets written up.
	</p>

	<h2>What you'll find here</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Practical systems for planning, shipping, and following through on projects</li>
		<li>Templates and tools you can copy and adapt in minutes, not hours</li>
		<li>Short, direct write-ups — respect for your time is part of the design</li>
		<li>Occasional deep dives when a topic genuinely needs the extra length</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Why "Buzzyfly"</h2>
	<p>
		Because the work that actually moves things forward rarely looks glamorous — it's the small,
		buzzing, unglamorous stuff done consistently. That's the whole philosophy in one word.
	</p>

	<h2>Get the dispatch</h2>
	<p>
		New posts, templates, and tools go out through the Buzzyfly Dispatch before anywhere else. If
		that sounds useful, you can <a href="/#subscribe">join the list</a> or start with the
		<a href="/blog">latest posts</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
